# Qwen3.8-27B, RedHatAI INT4 (LLM Compressor: AWQ smoothing + GPTQ, compressed-tensors W4A16,
# symmetric, group 128; DeltaNet in_proj_a/b, lm_head and embeddings stay bf16).
# The checkpoint declares an FP8 KV-cache scheme, which vLLM applies under --kv-cache-dtype=auto;
# --kv-cache-dtype=bfloat16 keeps the KV cache in bf16 like every other preset.
# Measured on an RTX 3090 (docs/research/candidates.md): 16.84 GiB weights, 2.88 GiB KV cache
# (28,912 tokens), ~140 s to healthy.
# Shared by the Qwen3.5-architecture candidate presets (docs/research/candidates.md): thinking off for every
# chat and /tokenize render (the template thinks by default); --language-model-only skips the
# vision tower; bf16 activations (the base model's dtype); --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 bounds
# echo's prompt-logprob spike (full 248k-vocab logits per prompt token of a chunk, not covered by
# vLLM's startup memory profile); --generation-config=vllm ignores the upload's sampling defaults.
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL=RedHatAI/Qwen3.8-27B-INT4
JEVEMU_VLLM_MODEL_REVISION=2f0fa48fea4949b56685ddfc48c05dd81c7d772b
JEVEMU_VLLM_DTYPE=bfloat16
JEVEMU_VLLM_MAX_MODEL_LEN=8192
JEVEMU_VLLM_GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.95
JEVEMU_VLLM_DEFAULT_CHAT_TEMPLATE_KWARGS='{"enable_thinking":false}'
JEVEMU_VLLM_EXTRA_ARGS='--language-model-only --max-num-seqs=16 --max-num-batched-tokens=1024 --generation-config=vllm --kv-cache-dtype=bfloat16'
